no time to die daniel craig's final  outing as james bond ties up a lot of  loose ends from his tenure on screen as  a renowned super spy when the dust  settles the day has been saved and this  era of bond has drawn to a close we  still have some unanswered questions  no time to die is a whopping 2 hours and  45 minutes long with a 30 minute opening  sequence the most stirring part of this  epic opening set piece comes when bond  at the behest of madeleine swann visits  the final resting place of west lind the  love interest who betrayed him in casino  royale madeleine wants to start a new  life with james and that requires  closing the chapters behind them for  madeleine that means telling james or  the secret she's never shared but for  james that means forgiving a dead woman  he still loves when he gets to her grave  it's been booby-trapped and explodes in  his face setting his quest in motion and  severing his trust with madeline who he  now believes must be vesper 2.0 having  lured him into this mess later in the  film blofeld confesses to bond that as  inspector he was the author of this  particular pain point knowing bond would  eventually visit her tomb and that's all  he had to do was bide his time what's  not explicitly spelled out is just how  long he had been planning this at that  point in the film blofeld has been in  prison for half a decade so did he have  his long distance henchmen rig up the  cemetery with explosives even before he  wound up incarcerated or were his men on  the outside just keeping tabs on bond  and the hopes and emotional ultimatum in  his relationship would lead to him being  at the right place at the wrong time  the film's opening flashback reveals a  fuller portrait of a plot point  originally revealed inspector that  madeleine's mother was killed by one of  her father mr white's enemies while she  was a child hiding upstairs here we see  that the enemy was new bond villain  lucifer saffin played by rami malik we  find out safin himself had his own  family brutally slaughtered by white so  his revenge was inevitable but when  madeleine as a child fights back against  his attack and he chases her to the  point she collapses under a frozen lake  safin chooses to rescue her in present  day after the five year time jump safin  reappears in madeleine's life and makes  her an unwitting pawn in his master plan  making it clear he's been obsessed with  her since that fateful day  you don't know what this is  but the film was built around the  premise that the full details of their  connection will prove devastating to  james in a way they do because madeline  and james have lost years of their lives  not even speaking because the plot's  circumstances convinced him she wasn't  to be trusted which couldn't be further  from the truth we just never find out  more about safin and madeline's  connection he must have taken her to  safety after retrieving her from under  the ice but did he help raise her for a  time he claims to have kept a close  watch on her over the years but was she  ever aware was there more to this shared  history or was it all just a misdirect  after appearing in both casino royale  and quantum of solace as franchise star  wars felix leiter bond's american bestie  played by jeffrey wright was nowhere to  be seen in the ensuing two sequels he  returns here as a catalyst for much of  the film's plot and when he does lighter  and bond seem even closer and chummier  than they did when he was still a brand  new double o this mission the two men  embark on together proves to be their  last as lighter dies in front of bond  drowning and suffering from gunshot  wounds from fellow spook logan ash who  betrayed them both it proves to be one  of the film's most affecting moments  largely because of the palpable  chemistry between craig and wright bond  being an international agent is presumed  he and leiter worked on many many unseen  missions in between his last appearance  and this film but we still wonder what  he was up to as a rogue former mi6 agent  rather murk in skyfall and the spectre  became such a powerful force for  terrorism  in a key moment in the film safin uses a  kidnapped mi6 scientist to alter a  weaponized disease blofeld was planning  to use to kill bond making it backfire  and kill every living member of spectre  this happens at a ball thrown for the  evil organization with blofeld in prison  attending via the connection from his  bionic eye to a mirrored one out in the  real world when bond has to explain to  him that blofeld has been orchestrating  spectre activities from behind bars  using his bionic eye em explains that no  one sees or speaks to blofeld all day  outside of his therapist madeline but  how did mi6 not notice this man had a  cybernetic science fiction eyeball for  the last five years  the film's primary mcguffin is project  heracles a bioweapon designed to only  affect genetically marked targets mi6  was developing it as an off the books  program that would make missions simpler  and risk fewer field agents lives  somehow m is surprised when it's stolen  by spectre then saturn's upstart  operation and repurposed as a weapon of  mass destruction in the film's climax  saffin's island existing in a nebulous  ungoverned space between russia and  japan must be destroyed to stop project  heracles from being deployed globally  he's going to kill millions m struggles  to navigate the quagmire strategically  because england can't be seen as  instigating an international incident  especially when the impetus behind it  would reveal gross negligence on their  parts so when the dust cleared how did  em avoid catastrophic geopolitical  blowback after destroying the island  with missiles as the remaining cast  eulogizes the fallen it certainly  appears em still has his job so he must  have executed some true diplomatic  finesse to keep his head  when no time to die and its lengthy  credits finally crawl to a close the  film's closing message is that james  bond will return but not only is daniel  craig not returning for another film his  iteration of james bond meets an  untimely end in a tragic scene of  self-sacrifice in the movie's final act  we know how this goes new bond actor  usually means new bond continuity but  we're in uncharted territory now that we  have a canonical bond film that shows  the hero dying at the end so with the  shauna lynch's nomi most likely  reclaiming her official designation as  double 07 after temporarily  relinquishing it to bond on his last  mission will she return in another film  just because the next bond film will  probably start from scratch doesn't mean  this particular world can't continue in  a spin-off sequel especially given the  warm reception to lynch's performance  and phoebe wore the bridge's exceptional  writing folks have been clamoring for a  female bond or a black bond in recent  years but perhaps now that lynch has  done such a fine job with nomi a black  female 07 why not give her a solo film  devoted to fleshing her out further  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  no time to die are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

